    "reason": "While '不同' can mean 'difference' in the sense of disparity or lack of uniformity/consistency (as in '品質の不同' - difference in quality/inconsistency), it is a more formal and specific term. For the general concept of 'difference' in daily life, '違い' (chigai) is the standard, most natural, and commonly used word. '不同' is too narrow and not the primary term a general learner would expect for this concept.",
